                                "sense_id": "710b4947-2bad-30a2-ac06-71f8b9a80bcc",
                                "text": "Up the RA!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6036dfac-a8b6-4d29-871b-2d33160b2647",
                                "sense_id": "710b4947-2bad-30a2-ac06-71f8b9a80bcc",
                                "text": "Good old Austin [ Currie ] was quick to say we hadn't and it wasn't a vote for the RA [ Republican Army ] ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ee28ae0-12cf-4643-9d44-a9bb6438c63d",
                                "sense_id": "710b4947-2bad-30a2-ac06-71f8b9a80bcc",
                                "text": "If he joins the RA he sees himself as a free man one day walking down the streets of New York."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9715157e-74b5-41dc-b478-c5d9167e1d51",
                                "sense_id": "710b4947-2bad-30a2-ac06-71f8b9a80bcc",
                                "text": "Aside from the RA inner core (of around 200 or so), AFA's periphery – not all of whom supported RA's Irish Republicanism – comprised students, anarchists, non-aligned anti-fascists, former hunt saboteurs, and even football casuals."
